# Netlify proxies /api/* to TokenRouter server-side, where CORS does not apply.
# TokenRouter answers the browser's preflight with 403 and no
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin, so a direct call from the page can only ever
# fail with "Failed to fetch". Status 200 makes this a rewrite, not a
# redirect, so the Authorization header survives the hop.
/api/*  https://api.tokenrouter.com/:splat  200
